WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.990
Speaker 1: Hey, David, is critical race theory
actually dangerous like right wingers say,

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:07.890
or is it just kind of reductive?

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.230
Yeah, this is good.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:15.300
You know, the I've issued many critiques about
critical race theory on this show.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.350
I don't think it's dangerous.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:25.099
I think as a general concept, one can always
argue being uninformed can have negative consequences.

00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:30.669
And so you could say, well, if you believe
that no matter how fast you drive, you won't

00:00:30.669 --> 00:00:32.480
get hurt if you get into a car crash.

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.859
Yeah, that's a belief that's dangerous in
a very specific and tangible way.

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:40.640
When it comes to critical race theory.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.329
I wouldn't apply the word dangerous.

00:00:42.329 --> 00:00:50.340
I, I do think, however, that critical race
theory could potentially be harmful to race

00:00:50.340 --> 00:00:52.239
relations between individuals.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:53.370
That's number one.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.969
I do think critical race theory is.

00:00:55.969 --> 00:01:03.850
Reductive in the way that it deals with race
over many other factors that affect how people

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:10.930
relate to each other in modern society, and
I've talked before about how, you know, critical

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:17.730
theories like critical race theory heavily
are supported by ideas of postmodernism and

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:19.049
post structuralism.

00:01:19.049 --> 00:01:23.380
And this is not me going all Jordan Peterson
talking about postmodernism.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.980
And that's not it's not this vague critique.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:33.350
And I'm not saying anything beyond what I'm
actually saying, but the basis of critical

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:40.600
race theory and the genesis of some of the
ideology and postmodernism and post structuralism

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:50.700
relies on the ideas in some combination that
reality is socially constructed.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:58.020
It's sort of an attack on empiricism and it's
a propping up of the idea that any reality,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:05.180
any notion, any analysis could be just as
real as any other and in some cases taken

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:13.930
to a very extreme place, could be deserves
equal footing in discussions about how society

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.120
should be organized.

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:20.510
And then one of the other aspects of critical
race theory that I think is very problematic

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.510
now.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.950
But by the way, if you're going to email me,
you're going to say, David, that one piece

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:27.790
doesn't apply to all of critical race theory.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:28.790
Fine.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:34.690
I'm talking in generalities about things that
exist within enclaves of critical race theory.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:44.510
One of the really concerning things I see
are very, very casual claims levied against

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:50.560
anyone who challenges aspects of critical
race theory that merely by challenging critical

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:56.900
race theory, you are a white supremacist,
you are racist, you are an oppressor.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:57.900
You are part of the problem.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.370
We saw this earlier this week with the story
about the Seattle Pride event, some pride

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:07.940
event in Seattle that was only going to charge
a fee to white people.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:09.510
How do you identify which those people are?

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:10.620
I don't know.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.140
And they weren't calling it an admission fee.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:18.940
They were calling it a reparations fee to
get around, saying the admission is is depending

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.810
on race.

00:03:20.810 --> 00:03:25.190
And then when some members of the Seattle
City Council said this, this is bad, this

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:27.170
really doesn't make any sense.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:34.240
They were accused of doing violence by critiquing
the plan of only charging the reparations

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.730
fee to the white attendees.

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:38.510
That's a that's a nonstarter for me.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.720
That's the opposite of rational inquiry.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.990
And so back to the question, is critical race
theory actually dangerous?

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:50.590
I think just about any idea if taken far enough,
you could justify and say it would be dangerous

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:52.130
in this way?

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:53.670
I think that it's incomplete.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.810
I think it's reductive.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:04:00.620
And I think it's counterproductive over the
long term to both race relations and achieving

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:06.450
real equality under the law and and in society,
which I think is an important add on, because

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:11.670
many areas we have equality under the law,
but for socio cultural reasons, we don't have

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:12.910
actual equality.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.030
That's my sense.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:14.950
Let me know your thoughts

